  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Chef gives you an array A=[A1,A2,…,AN]A = [A_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_N]A=[A1​,A2​,…,AN​] of length NNN.\n\nLet f(S)f(S)f(S) denote the bitwise OR of a non-empty subset SSS of AAA.\n\nFind the maximum possible value of f(S1)⊕f(S2)f(S_1) \\oplus f(S_2)f(S1​)⊕f(S2​) across all ways to **partition** the elements of AAA into two non-empty subsets S1S_1S1​ and S2S_2S2​.\n\nHere, ⊕\\oplus⊕ denotes the bitwise XOR operator.\n\nNote that you must partition AAA, i.e, every element of AAA must belong to either S1S_1S1​ or S2S_2S2​.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nFirst line of the input contains a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of two lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN, denoting the length of the array.\nThe second line of each test case contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​ —  the elements of array AAA.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, print the maximum possible value of f(S1)⊕f(S2)f(S_1) \\oplus f(S_2)f(S1​)⊕f(S2​) across all partitions of AAA into S1S_1S1​ and S2S_2S2​.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤4⋅1041 \\leq T \\leq 4 \\cdot 10^41≤T≤4⋅104",
      "2≤N≤2⋅1052 \\leq N \\leq 2 \\cdot 10^52≤N≤2⋅105",
      "0≤Ai&lt;2300 \\leq A_i \\lt 2^{30} 0≤Ai​&lt;230",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 2⋅1052 \\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n4\n1 3 7 15\n4\n1 1 2 2\n2\n3 4",
        "output": "14\n3\n7",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: The given array is [1,3,7,15][ 1 , 3 , 7 , 15 ][1,3,7,15].\nChoose S1={1}S_1 = \\{1\\}S1​={1} and S2={3,7,15}S_2 = \\{3, 7, 15\\}S2​={3,7,15} to obtain f(S1)=1f(S_1) = 1f(S1​)=1 and f(S2)=3∣7∣15=15f(S_2) = 3\\mid 7\\mid 15 = 15f(S2​)=3∣7∣15=15, giving us f(S1)⊕f(S2)=14f(S_1) \\oplus f(S_2) = 14f(S1​)⊕f(S2​)=14.\nYou may verify that no other partition gives a larger value.\nTest case 222: The given array is [1,1,2,2][ 1 , 1 ,2 , 2 ][1,1,2,2].\nChoose S1={1,1}S_1 = \\{1, 1\\}S1​={1,1} and S2={2,2}S_2 = \\{2, 2\\}S2​={2,2} to obtain f(S1)⊕f(S2)=3f(S_1) \\oplus f(S_2) = 3f(S1​)⊕f(S2​)=3, which is the maximum possible.\nTest case 333: The given array is [3,4][ 3 , 4 ][3,4].\nWe have no choice: any partition will give us 3⊕4=73\\oplus 4 = 73⊕4=7."
      }
    ]
  },
